# =============================================================================
# Security perimeter for the Claude auto-review pipeline.
# =============================================================================
# These paths control whether and how secret-bearing CI runs against PR
# content (LLM Gateway credentials are exposed to the review job, and the
# post job runs with pull-requests: write). A PR that modifies any of these
# paths can in principle disable the controls that protect those secrets:
# the --allowedTools restriction, the overlay step, the sanitizer, the
# two-job split. The wildcard above already requires a code owner review
# on these paths; the explicit entries below exist to make that requirement
# inspectable, to survive any future change to the wildcard rule, and as
# the obvious place to add additional reviewers (e.g. a security team) if
# one is later established.
#
# IMPORTANT for maintainers: CODEOWNERS gates MERGE, not workflow EXECUTION.
# The Claude auto-review workflow runs on the PR (not on the post-merge
# commit), so a maintainer applying the `claude-review` label on a PR that
# touches these paths is running the PR's modified version with secrets in
# env. Always inspect the diff in these paths before applying the label.
# When in doubt, use the workflow_dispatch escape hatch instead -- it runs
# from the default branch's already-reviewed copy of the workflow.
.github/workflows/  @causten
.github/scripts/    @causten
.claude/            @causten
